{% comment %}
  Gallery Lookbook popup shell — rendered once per section.

  Every media block used to render its own <lookbook-popup>, so a gallery of N cards shipped N
  popups (and 4N when desktop and mobile layouts differ, since the block list is printed once per
  layout tree). Only one can ever be open, so the section now renders this single shell and each
  trigger carries its card's body in a <template>; gallery-lookbook.js copies that template into
  [lookbook-popup-content] just before the popup opens. Same pattern as the quiz support guide
  drawer (snippets/quiz-support-guide-drawer.liquid).

  Everything here is section-level and never changes between cards — heading, close button, the
  Full width class. Only the media column and the product list are per-block, and those are what
  the template replaces.

  Accepts:
  - section: {Object} the Gallery Lookbook section
{% endcomment %}

<lookbook-popup
  drawer-type="lookbook-popup-{{ section.id }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    data-section-id traces this popup back to its section once JS has moved it to <body>: the
    editor re-renders the section, not the portal, so that is the only way to find the copy left
    behind when the section stops rendering a popup.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    The popup is portaled to <body>, so it cannot inherit the section's .container — carry the
    Full width setting across as a class instead, for the inset media on mobile.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  class="lookbook-popup{% unless section.settings.full_width %} lookbook-popup--contained{% endunless %}"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <div class="lookbook-popup__overlay position-absolute" drawer-overlay></div>
  <div class="lookbook-popup__dialog color-{{ settings.drawer_color_scheme }}">
    <div class="lookbook-popup__header d-flex align-item-center justify-content-space-btw flex-shrink-0">
      {%- if section.settings.popup_heading != blank -%}
        <{{ section.settings.popup_heading_tag }}
          class="{{ section.settings.popup_heading_size }} fnt-heading lookbook-popup__heading m-0"
          style="color: {{ section.settings.popup_text_color }}"
        >
          {{ section.settings.popup_heading }}
        </{{ section.settings.popup_heading_tag }}>
      {%- endif -%}
      <button
        class="lookbook-popup__close cursor-pointer"
        type="button"
        close-drawer
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close_drawer' | t }}"
      >
        {%- render 'icon' with 'drawerclose-icon' -%}
      </button>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%}
      Filled from the trigger's <template> on open — image column + product column. Empty until
      then, which is why the popup is only ever reachable through a trigger that carries one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="lookbook-popup__layout" lookbook-popup-content></div>
  </div>
</lookbook-popup>
